The **Lead Details Page** provides a complete view of an individual lead, including contact information, activity history, files, and internal notes. This page acts as the central workspace for managing and nurturing a lead until it is converted into a client or deal.

## Purpose

The Lead Details Page helps you:

- View complete lead information in one place
- Track interaction history and updates
- Manage lead data and context
- Store related files and notes
- Convert leads into clients when qualified

## How to Access

1. Go to **Leads**
1. Click on any lead from the list

![](image.png)

3. You will be redirected to the **Lead Details Page**

## Page Layout

The page is divided into two main sections:

### 3.1 Left Panel — Lead Information

### 3.2 Right Panel — Activity & Records

# Header Section

At the top of the page, you will see:

### Lead Name

- Displays the full name of the lead
- Example: *Macaulay Arnold*

### Website

- Shows the lead’s associated website (if available)

### Action Buttons (Top Right)

- **Email Icon**
  - Quickly send an email to the lead

![](image.png)

- **Call Icon**
  - Initiate or log a phone call (requires Twilio configuration)
- **Convert To Client**
  - Converts the lead into a client record
  - Used when the lead is qualified

![](image.png)

# Left Panel — About This Lead

This section contains structured lead information.

## Contact Information

Includes:

- Website
- Phone number
- Email address

This allows quick communication and reference.

## Address

Displays location details such as:

- Zip Code
- (Other fields like Country, State, City if available)

## Description

A text field that contains:

- Notes about the lead
- Requirements or context
- Internal observations

## Last Modified

Shows:

- Date and time of the last update
- Helps track recent activity or changes

# Right Panel — Activity & Records

This section manages all interactions and supporting data.

## 6.1 Tabs

### Timeline (Default)

- Displays a chronological history of events
- Example:
  - Lead created
  - Updates made
  - Activities logged

### Files

- Stores uploaded documents related to the lead
- Examples:
  - Attachments
  - Proposals
  - Shared files

### Notes

- Internal notes for team collaboration
- Not visible to the lead
- Useful for tracking discussions or decisions

# Timeline Section

The Timeline provides:

- Date-based activity grouping
- Timestamps for each action
- User attribution (who performed the action)

### Example Entry:

- Created by [User Name]
- Time of creation

# Key Features

## Centralized Information

All lead-related data is stored in one place for easy access.

## Activity Tracking

Every update is recorded in the timeline for transparency.

## Quick Actions

Email, call, and conversion actions are accessible from the top.

## Conversion Ready

Leads can be converted into clients directly from this page.

# Lead Conversion

### Convert to Client

- Moves the lead into the client database
- Retains important information
- Typically used after qualification

# Workflow Example

1. User opens a lead
1. Reviews contact details and description
1. Logs interaction or adds notes
1. Uploads relevant files
1. Tracks activity in timeline
1. Clicks **Convert To Client** when ready

# Best Practices

- Keep lead information updated
- Add notes after every interaction
- Use timeline to track engagement
- Attach relevant files for context
- Convert leads only after proper qualification
